mkfs fails when its writes do

ext4_mkfs builds the entire filesystem in write-back mode, which makes its
teardown the write path: ext4_fs_fini writes the superblock, and leaving
write-back mode (ext4_block_cache_write_back(bd, 0)) flushes everything
else. Both results were discarded -- the exit sequence runs fs_fini,
cache-off, bcache_fini, block_fini and returns whatever r held from the
build phase, so a format whose flushes failed still reported success.

In practice two other nets usually catch a dying medium first: mkfs
re-opens its own volume mid-format and verifies (patch 0024), so a block
that reads back wrong fails the build phase; and patch 0033's latch makes
the final cache flush return the swallowed error -- to this call site,
which then dropped it. The bad-sector injection that motivated this patch
was caught by the verification pass even before 0033. What remained open
is exactly the gap between those nets: a write that fails after the last
verification read, on a block verification does not cover. "newfs
reported success" has to mean the writes landed, not that the failure
happened to be somewhere the safety nets look.

Both results now merge into the return, first error wins, teardown still
runs to the end.

diff --git a/src/ext4_mkfs.c b/src/ext4_mkfs.c
--- a/src/ext4_mkfs.c
+++ b/src/ext4_mkfs.c
@@ -964,10 +964,25 @@ int ext4_mkfs(struct ext4_fs *fs, struct ext4_blockdev *bd,
 		goto fs_fini;
 
 	fs_fini:
-	ext4_fs_fini(fs);
+	{
+		/* Teardown IS the write path here: the whole filesystem was
+		 * built in write-back mode, fs_fini writes the superblock and
+		 * leaving write-back mode flushes everything else. Their
+		 * results were discarded, so a format whose writes never
+		 * landed still reported success -- "created ext4 volume"
+		 * over a medium holding nothing of the sort. The first error
+		 * wins; teardown still runs to the end. */
+		int fr = ext4_fs_fini(fs);
+		if (r == EOK)
+			r = fr;
+	}
 
 	cache_fini:
-	ext4_block_cache_write_back(bd, 0);
+	{
+		int cr = ext4_block_cache_write_back(bd, 0);
+		if (r == EOK)
+			r = cr;
+	}
 	ext4_bcache_fini_dynamic(&bc);
 
 	block_fini:
